A||||2||wardog85GT||Has anyone ever cut the stock coil springs? How does it ride?||||1||
Z||000000||wardog85GT||09-18-2001||08:55 PM||||Has anyone out there ever cut their stock coil springs? If so, how much did you cut off and how much did it lower it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||09-18-2001||09:57 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013495.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013495.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013276.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013276.html</A> <P>and many other past posts.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||09-19-2001||02:16 AM||||If you cut your springs the spring rate will increase. To compensate for this start with a lower rate spring. I used 4 cyl 88 coupe springs with 1 coil removed in place of my stock 88 GT higher rate front springs. My ride actually improved and the car no longer has the nose high look of stock 88's. The front suspension takes broken pavement much better with the softer coupe spring even with 1 coil removed. This is with 17 in wheels and tires.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||3
